{"id": "DeO-kXpxzdW", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why does Maa Durga have TEN arms? 🔱 And what happened when Mahishasura turned into a LION… right in front of HER lion? 🦁 Part 2\n\nMahishasura had a powerful boon: no god or man could kill him.\n\nSo the gods joined their powers, and from their divine light emerged someone who was neither.\n\nMaa Durga. 🔱\n\nThen, every god gave her a weapon:\n\n🔱 Shiva — trishul \n🌀 Vishnu — chakra \n⚡ Indra — vajra \n🐚 Varuna — shankh \n🏹 Vayu — bow & arrows \n…and Himavan, the mountain king, gave her something very special: her LION. 🦁\n\nMahishasura fought her in many forms — a buffalo, a lion, an elephant and a buffalo again.\n\nNine nights of battle.\n\nNAVRATRI. 🌙\n\nAnd on the tenth day, Maa Durga defeated him.\n\nVIJAYADASHAMI. 🙏\n\nSo those ten arms aren't just about looking powerful. They represent the many divine weapons and powers Maa Durga received to defeat evil.\n\n📚 Meet Maa's forms in the Rishi Katha picture books: Books 1–3 — Shailputri, Brahmacharini & Chandraghanta.\n\n3 books · ₹500 · rishikatha.com \n(Link in bio)\n\nTag the DURGA of your house 🔱 — the one who fixes EVERYTHING. 😂\n\nAnd save this for Navratri 📌\n\n#RishiKatha #Navratri #Navratri2026 #MaaDurga #DurgaPuja #Mahishasura #MahishasuraMardini #Vijayadashami #Dussehra #JaiMataDi #IndianMythology #KidsBooks #HinduMythologyForKids #ParentingIndia #IndianParents", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1791464026, "like_count": 12850, "comment_count": 53, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-2145035156097810a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 55.085, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQMpL3uKBK4320eNdK14Fs26G9ylH5JpvneOa8gZeOUc8G7r8F5brtIBZC6zMSTgRgbDFUM9veupso9n9zOqwVlPlGclhN5DfhHV4gc.mp4?_nc_cat